# Boot steps 6, 7 and 9 (docs/design.md, "Boot"): the boot plan, the
# untyped, BootInfo and the root CNode pass l4core::boot::check's checks,
# and every untyped descriptor is clear of kernel memory as the kernel's
# arch code finds it from the CPU's registers, the linker's symbols and
# the live page tables: the kernel image and what lies in it, the device
# window's pages, the boot region, the MSI window and the low 1 MiB. Every
# RAM untyped is RAM the kernel hands out. A walk of the live direct map
# finds every RAM untyped mapped write-back and no device untyped in a
# write-back page (ADR 0004).
cmdline: test=bootinfo
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: cmdline: "test=bootinfo"
expect: bootinfo: boot region
expect: bootinfo: check_plan: ok
expect: bootinfo: check_untyped: ok
expect: bootinfo: check_bootinfo: ok
expect: bootinfo: check_root_cnode: ok
expect: bootinfo: the kernel image is
expect: bootinfo: the kernel stack at
expect: bootinfo: the PML4 in CR3 at
expect: are clear of the kernel image, its 12 parts above, 3 device-window pages, the boot region, the MSI window and [0, 1 MiB)
expect: bootinfo: every RAM untyped is RAM the kernel hands out
expect: bootinfo: the live direct map maps every RAM untyped write-back and no device untyped write-back
expect: TEST PASS
